   "source": [
    "## Cell 2 — Box–Muller Method\n",
    "\n",
    "For independent uniform random variables \\(U_1, U_2 \\in (0,1)\\), the Box–Muller transformation gives\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Z_0 = \\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\cos(2\\pi U_2)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Z_1 = \\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\sin(2\\pi U_2)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The resulting values are independent standard normal samples, each following \\(N(0,1)\\). Each iteration produces two values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "8ed2b3ea",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.974997Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.974766Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.978971Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.978228Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def box_muller(n):\n",
    "    values = []\n",
    "    while len(values) < n:\n",
    "        u1 = random.random()\n",
    "        u2 = random.random()\n",
    "        while u1 == 0.0:\n",
    "            u1 = random.random()\n",
    "        radius = math.sqrt(-2.0 * math.log(u1))\n",
    "        angle = 2.0 * math.pi * u2\n",
    "        values.extend([\n",
    "            radius * math.cos(angle),\n",
    "            radius * math.sin(angle)\n",
    "        ])\n",
    "    return np.array(values[:n], dtype=float)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76f6e518",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cell 3 — Generate 2D Gaussian Samples \n",
    "\n",
    "For a symmetric positive-definite covariance matrix, use the eigendecomposition\n",
    "\n",
    "$$C = V\\Lambda V^T$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and generate samples as\n",
    "\n",
    "$$X = Z\\Lambda^{1/2}V^T + \\mu.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This works for spherical, diagonal, and full covariance matrices."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "bb9930b8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.980368Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.980241Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.983785Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-15T14:38:44.983447Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def generate_2d_gaussian(n, mean, covariance):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generate N(mu, C) samples with eigendecomposition, not Cholesky.\"\"\"\n",
    "    mean = np.asarray(mean, dtype=float)\n",
    "    covariance = np.asarray(covariance, dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if covariance.shape != (2, 2):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Covariance matrix must be 2x2.\")\n",
    "    if not np.allclose(covariance, covariance.T, atol=1e-9):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Covariance matrix must be symmetric.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    eigenvalues, eigenvectors = np.linalg.eigh(covariance)\n",
    "    if np.any(eigenvalues <= 0):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Covariance matrix must be positive definite.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    z = np.column_stack((box_muller(n), box_muller(n)))\n",
    "    transform = eigenvectors @ np.diag(np.sqrt(eigenvalues))\n",
    "    return z @ transform.T + mean\n"
   ]
  },
