    "## Observations and conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Box–Muller transforms uniform random values into standard normal samples.\n",
    "2. The Gaussian generator uses covariance eigendecomposition; no Cholesky decomposition is used.\n",
    "3. Each class is generated from three Gaussian components with mixture weights 0.40, 0.20, and 0.40.\n",
    "4. Spherical covariance creates circular clouds; diagonal covariance creates axis-aligned ellipses; full covariance permits correlated, tilted ellipses.\n",
    "5. K-Means partitions the training data for each class into two nearest-centroid regions.\n",
    "6. The distortion classifier predicts the class with the smaller minimum squared distance to its class-specific centroids.\n",
    "7. Report the measured test accuracy and confusion matrix printed when the notebook is run."
   ]
